# Build context exclusions.
#
# The build context is the repository root (the backend image needs
# `knowledge_base/` and `prompts/`), so everything that must never reach an
# image is excluded here.

# --- version control ---------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore

# --- secrets: never bake an env file into an image ---------------------------
# `env_file` in docker-compose feeds the container at RUNTIME, from the host.
# Nothing env-shaped belongs in the build context.
#
# The two bare patterns below only cover the build-context ROOT. Nested files
# such as `apps/web/.env.local` were therefore NOT excluded — a real gap that
# this project already hit once: `API_PROXY_TARGET` in that file is read by
# Next at build time and gets baked into the image, silently pointing the proxy
# at 127.0.0.1. The `**/` forms close it for every depth.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
*.pem

# --- python ------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv
venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
backend/data
**/*.sqlite3

# --- node --------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/out
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# --- docs / artefacts --------------------------------------------------------
# NOTE: `legacy/` is intentionally NOT excluded — the compose `legacy` profile
# builds `legacy/Dockerfile` with this same context. It is never started by
# default (profile-gated), but it must stay buildable.
docs/images
tmp
deploy_package
*.log

# --- os ----------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
